{%- comment -%}
  PG Sellout Last: move the "Sellout risk: HIGH" card to sit directly under the
  last bundle tile — "Buy 5, Get 3 FREE" — per the owner: it is the closing
  line of the upsell ladder, not an intro to it.

  WHERE IT WAS. pg-landing renders the card between the review quote and the
  BUNDLE & SAVE divider, so it read as a preamble to the tiles. On phones
  pg-tiktok-pdp then moves it further away again, into the full-width
  #pg-tt-below container under the photo/tiles grid, alongside the info row and
  the accordions.

  HOW IT MOVES. The card is put inside a wrapper, .pg-sell-slot, inserted right
  after the last .pgx-lad tile. The wrapper is the point, not decoration:

    - pg-tiktok-pdp's relocate() collects `:scope > .pgx-sellout` — a DIRECT
      child of .pgx-buy — every 900ms and on every mutation. Nested one level
      down, the card no longer matches, so the two do not fight over it. Any
      placeholder relocate() may already have left behind is an empty hidden
      <i> and harmless.
    - pg-tiktok-pdp's mobile flex ordering works on direct children too
      (`#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-sellout{order:9}` put it after the quote). The
      wrapper takes that seat instead, at order 6: after the tiles (4) and the
      add-to-cart row (5), before the quote (8).

  The anchor is the LAST .pgx-lad in the DOM, whatever that is: pgLadder builds
  Single / Buy 2 Get 1, then pg-tile-copy appends Buy 4 Get 2 and Buy 5 Get 3,
  and both rebuild the ladder from scratch on their own intervals. So the pass
  re-runs, is idempotent (it only touches the DOM when the slot is not already
  seated after the last tile), and simply waits when no tile is on screen yet.

  ON A PAGE WITH NO LADDER it falls back to pg-landing's own tiles. The R36S is
  in pgLadder's NO_LADDER list (its volume pricing needs BXGY discounts that do
  not exist for it), so there the last tile is the "Bundle Deal: 2x" one that
  pg-landing renders itself. The fallback is only consulted when no .pgx-lad is
  on the page at all, so on the orb it never fires once the ladder is up — and
  while the ladder is still being built, a first placement after the native tile
  is corrected by the next pass.

  Desktop has no flex ordering on that column, so the DOM position does the
  work there and the result is the same: the card lands under the final tile.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  #pgx .pgx-buy > .pg-sell-slot{order:6;margin:14px 0 0}
  #pgx .pg-sell-slot .pgx-sellout{margin-bottom:0}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgSelloutLast) return; window.pgSelloutLast = 1;

  function place(){
    var sell = document.querySelector('#pgx .pgx-sellout');
    if (!sell) return;
    var tiles = document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-lad');
    /* no ladder on this product (R36S): use pg-landing's own tiles */
    if (!tiles.length) tiles = document.querySelectorAll('#pgx .pgx-buy > .pgx-tile');
    if (!tiles.length) return;                       /* nothing to sit under yet */
    var last = tiles[tiles.length - 1];
    if (!last.parentNode) return;

    var slot = document.querySelector('#pgx .pg-sell-slot');
    if (!slot){
      slot = document.createElement('div');
      slot.className = 'pg-sell-slot';
    }
    /* only touch the DOM when it is not already where it belongs */
    if (slot.parentNode !== last.parentNode || slot.previousElementSibling !== last){
      last.parentNode.insertBefore(slot, last.nextSibling);
    }
    if (sell.parentNode !== slot) slot.appendChild(sell);
  }

  function boot(){
    place();
    var root = document.getElementById('pgx');
    if (root && window.MutationObserver){
      var q = false;
      /* pgLadder and pg-tile-copy both rebuild the tiles from scratch */
      new MutationObserver(function(){
        if (q) return;
        q = true;
        setTimeout(function(){ q = false; place(); }, 80);
      }).observe(root, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    }
    setInterval(place, 900);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
